"Têbêts","d":"Tebets, a place in Palestine","p":"tay-bates'","t":"tebets","g":"Thebez","fb":[["thebez","Thebez","","Abimelech, Gideon's son who made himself king, was besieging the tower at Thebez when a woman dropped a millstone on his head. He told his armor-bearer to kill him so nobody could say a woman did it. Joab still remembered it years later.","place",2]],"v":[6804,6804,8280]},"H8459":{"l":"תֹּחוּ","x":"Tôchûw","d":"Tochu, an Israelite","p":"to'-khoo","t":"tochu","g":"of Tohu","fb":[["tohu","Tohu","Levite living at the time of United Monarchy","Several generations back in Samuel's family line, before his father Elkanah.","person",1]],"v":[7213]},"H8427":{"l":"תָּוָה","x":"tâvâh","d":"to mark out, i.e. (primitive) scratch or (definite) imprint","p":"taw-vaw'","t":"tavah","g":"he made marks","fb":[],"v":[7785,20625]},"H8461":{"l":"תַּחְכְּמֹנִי","x":"Tachkᵉmônîy","d":"Tachkemoni, an Israelite","p":"takh-kem-o-nee'","t":"tachkemoni","g":"a Tahkemonite","fb":[["tachmonite","Tachmonite","People, perhaps from Hachmon or Tahchemon","It is Jashobeam's family name, and he was chief of David's three mightiest warriors. 2 Samuel 23:8 credits him with eight hundred men killed at one time. Chronicles spells it Hachmonite.","group",1]],"v":[8661]},"H8483":{"l":"תַּחְתִּים חׇדְשִׁי","x":"Tachtîym Chodshîy","d":"Tachtim-Chodshi, a place in Palestine","p":"takh-teem' khod-shee'","t":"tachtim chodshi","g":"Tahtim Hodshi","fb":[["tahtim-hodshi","Tahtim-hodshi","Kadesh","It turns up once, on Joab's census route east of the Jordan, somewhere north of Gilead. The Hebrew is hard to read here, and many think it is a garbled reference to the Hittites of Kadesh and not a town at all.","place",1]],"v":[8698,8698]},"H8412":{"l":"תַּדְמֹר","x":"Tadmôr","d":"Tadmor, a place near Palestine","p":"tad-more'","t":"tadmor","g":"Tadmor","fb":[["tadmor","Tadmor","","It was Solomon's city out in the desert northeast of Damascus, on the caravan routes, and the Greeks and Romans knew it as Palmyra.","place",2]],"v":[9069,11350]},"H8472":{"l":"תַּחְפְּנֵיס","x":"Tachpᵉnêyç","d":"Tachpenes, an Egyptian woman","p":"takh-pen-ace'","t":"tachpeneyc","g":"of Tahpenes","fb":[["tahpenes","Tahpenes","Woman living at the time of United Monarchy","She was Pharaoh's queen in Egypt when Hadad the Edomite fled there from Solomon. Pharaoh gave Hadad her sister as his wife, and Tahpenes raised their son in the palace.","person",2]],"v":[9127,9128,9128]},"H8402":{"l":"תִּבְנִי","x":"Tibnîy","d":"Tibni, an Israelite","p":"tib-nee'","t":"tibni","g":"Tibni","fb":[["tibni","Tibni","Man living at the time of Divided Monarchy","After Zimri died, half of Israel followed Tibni son of Ginath and half followed Omri. It went on for four years. Then Tibni died and Omri was king.","person",2]],"v":[9304,9305,9305]},"H8466":{"l":"תַּחֲנָה","x":"tachănâh","d":"(only plural collectively) an encampment","p":"takh-an-aw'","t":"tachanah","g":"encampment","fb":[],"v":[9682]},"H8407":{"l":"תִּגְלַת פִּלְאֶסֶר","x":"Tiglath Pilʼeçer","d":"Tiglath-Pileser or Tilgath-pilneser, an Assyryrian king","p":"tig-lath' pil-eh'-ser","t":"tiglath pilecer","g":"Tiglath-pileser","fb":[["tiglath-pileser","Tiglath-pileser","King living at the time of Divided Monarchy","He was the third Assyrian king of the name, and he took territory from Israel and Syria and collected tribute. His own inscriptions record the same campaigns and payments 2 Kings describes.","person",6]],"v":[9954,9954,9970,9970,9973,9973,10434,10434,10454,10454,11784,11784]},"H8433":{"l":"תּוֹכֵחָה","x":"tôwkêchâh","d":"chastisement; figuratively (by words) correction, refutation, proof (even in defence)","p":"to-kay-khaw'","t":"tokechah","g":"rebuke","fb":[],"v":[10064,13158,13422,14503,14522,15033,16391,16422,16424,16429,16465,16528,16562,16672,16719,16764,16811,16816,16837,16838,17173,17224,17238,18354,20560,21099,22160,22748]},"H8488":{"l":"תֵּימְנִי","x":"Têymᵉnîy","d":"Temeni, an Israelite","p":"tay-men-ee'","t":"teymeni","g":"Temeni","fb":